Program 2: Function with parameters and no return value
This method takes two numbers and prints their sum.
public class Addition {

    // Function with parameters
    void add(int a, int b) {
        int sum = a + b;
        System.out.println("Sum = " + sum);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Addition obj = new Addition();

        // Passing arguments
        obj.add(10, 20);
    }
}
Output
Sum = 30
Explanation
•	The method add(int a, int b) receives two parameters.
•	The values 10 and 20 are passed as arguments.
•	The method calculates the sum and prints it.
